WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:07.920
In Iran tens of thousands have taken to
the streets in a massive countrywide uprising.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.480
Dozens have been killed and
hundreds arrested.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.040
Most demonstrations in

00:00:15.059 --> 00:00:19.560
Iran historically have started in the
capital, organized by educated upper

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.490
middle class and politically active
citizens. The protests then spread

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:27.240
outward from there, but the most recent
demonstrations started in the east of

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.860
the country, far from Tehran. They then
spread to the rest of the country within days.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.489
And they were started by working
middle-class Iranians, without a leader

00:00:35.489 --> 00:00:39.390
or a set agenda. And the match that lit
this fire was something that may

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:41.960
surprise you: the price of eggs.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.260
Iran was recently hit

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:49.440
with an outbreak of the bird flu, which
required them to kill off some

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:53.640
17 million chickens. This shortage caused
egg prices to nearly double.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:02.560
Egg prices helped spark the uprising, but what Iranians are really protesting here is a

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:06.480
series of broken promises by their
President, Hassan Rouhani.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:26.500
When Rouhani came into the presidency in 2013, he pledged to revitalize the economy. He took the first

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:30.350
steps towards doing this in July 2015,
when Iran reached a deal to

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:34.010
significantly curb its nuclear program.
In exchange, the West lifted

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:38.500
international economic sanctions that
had hampered Iran's economy for decades.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:44.480
For a lot of Iranians, this symbolized
that Iran was opening up to the world

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:48.980
and it was a reason to celebrate. So by
the end of Rouhani's first term, he had

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:52.760
achieved some economic success. His
policies had brought down the inflation

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:56.540
rate and boosted economic growth, but
unemployment and inequality remained

00:01:56.540 --> 00:02:00.800
high and foreign investments still
remained low. For the working poor Rouhani's

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:04.610
policies made little difference.
So when Rouhani was back up for election

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:08.420
in May 2017, he vowed to voters that he would make

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:12.360
tangible changes to the economy within
the first hundred days of his new term.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.340
He won the election, but the first hundred days came

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:27.460
and went with no real tangible economic
results.

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:29.780
I as an Iranian, am frustrated

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:34.580
that government has so many unkept
promises, to tackle so many problems like

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:38.060
unemployment, recession, inflation, and
social freedom.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:39.770
Then in December, Rouhani

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:42.540
published his proposal for his 2018
budget.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:45.440
The proposal included plans to

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:48.920
give billions of dollars to
organizations that make up the hardline

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:52.280
religious establishment in Iran. The
budget also proposed cutting cash

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:56.510
subsidies to millions of citizens,
raising the fuel prices, and privatizing

00:02:56.510 --> 00:03:01.100
public schools. Paired with the rising
prices of eggs and other food staples,

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:05.600
people around the country, especially the
poor and working-class, felt betrayed.

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:18.620
Protests erupted, quickly turning violent.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:29.420
These protesters have no leader, no set
agenda. They're not driven by political

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:34.620
organizers in the capital, but by poor
citizens and villages in rural towns.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:49.440
Iran has a history of massive street
protests transforming its society.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:54.220
In fact, the current Islamic Republic of
Iran was born by street protests just like this.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:59.160
These demonstrations began
because of the slow economy and the

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:04.880
price of eggs, but they quickly have
morphed into calls for reform and revolution.

